; spell.providers — the AGENT cluster: the LLM loop.
; STATUS: contract stub. Blocked by BOUNDARY (EDN cassettes) and one
; open question (:httpc under Mix — PLAN-017: works under `elixir -e`,
; fails under `mix run`, :http_util not on code path; root-cause before
; choosing transport).
;
; What deletes vs spell.jank's providers.jank:
;   curl + jq + json-escape + hex4   → :httpc (or curl Port) + :json
;   sqlite3 shell-out for agent.db   → sqlite via Port (boundary-safe;
;                                      credentials are low-throughput)
;   sha256sum for cassette keys      → :crypto.hash (verified)
;   cassette temp-file dance         → EDN cassettes via BOUNDARY —
;                                      one format for the whole system
;   PAINT-BEFORE-BLOCKING            → nothing. The call is a fenced
;                                      process; the window renders
;                                      throughout. The hand-drawn
;                                      "thinking…" frame was a
;                                      one-thread artifact.
;
; ── Contract ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; (register-providers!) → :registered
;   Populate STORE's :registry cell: provider-id →
;   {:ask fn :default-model "…"}. Data, not code sprinkled with defs.
;
; (load-credential provider-id) → {:kind :oauth :access … :refresh …
;   :expires …} | {:error msg}. Replay mode returns the cassette stub.
;   Read fresh each call (rotation-tolerant, as in jank).
;
; (ask provider-id cred prompt model) → {:ok text} | {:error msg}
;   One API call. Runs inside spell.fence/fence with a generous
;   deadline — HTTP gets a deadline here because the UI no longer
;   shares a thread with it (the jank carve-out inverts).
;
; (eval-tool! code) → printable-string
;   The agent's tool: BOUNDARY-read the code, FENCE the eval on a
;   SCRATCH namespace (or a separate node — the sandbox PLAN-017
;   verified: distribution works, so a model's (System/halt) kills a
;   scratch node, not the harness). Truncate output at 4000 chars.
;
; (agent-ask history prompt) → {:log [...] :reply text}
;   The multi-turn tool loop: call → if tool_use, eval-tool! and
;   recur → else reply. Bounded by max-turns (8), exactly as in jank —
;   the bound is a policy, and policy survives the port.
;
; Cassette layer: SPELL_CASSETTE / SPELL_CASSETTE_MODE env, modes
; record | replay | auto. REPLAY fails loud on a miss; auto demotes to
; network — jank's documented permissiveness, kept deliberately: the
; test suite depends on auto's demotion being visible in the cassette
; log.

(ns spell.providers)
